          "sha256": "2efed1125b8ee2313b4eeb83f998503d2b1831edd824bb8b8d2f2c47c3579cc3"
        }
      ],
      "notes": "23 October 2026 — Patch B, E-023: 53 targeted tests passed. Both import toolbars expose Download Result when a result exists for the current unlocked operator/database. Save cancellation/failure keeps that bounded in-memory artifact. There is no Retry Import action. Correctable failed XLSX retains original identifiers, physical rows, instruction rows, create/update choices and Stock; Import Results contains diagnostics and is not business data. Unsafe/corrupt/oversized files use a diagnostic-only XLSX and require correcting the original file or a fresh template. Ambiguous outcomes first read the original durable key; unresolved outcomes omit business input and warn against stock resubmission. Lock/disposal/database changes invalidate old artifacts and stale work. Success output behavior and import handlers/parsers/templates/schema/stock/pricing rules remain unchanged. Headless layout and event tests do not verify native OS dialogs or shop acceptance."
    },
